WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.922 --> 00:00:08.467
-(BUZZ SAW SCREECHING)
-♪ (OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING) ♪

2
00:00:12.387 --> 00:00:14.014
(DOG GROWLING)

3
00:00:17.768 --> 00:00:19.269
(SNARLS. HUFFS)

4
00:00:28.779 --> 00:00:30.739
♪ (MUSIC RISES) ♪

5
00:00:30.822 --> 00:00:33.575
(ZOMBIE SNARLS. GROANS)

6
00:00:34.910 --> 00:00:36.954
♪ (MUSIC INTENSIFIES) ♪

7
00:00:47.923 --> 00:00:49.633
-Hey. Stuart.
-♪ (MUSIC CONCLUDES) ♪

8
00:00:49.716 --> 00:00:50.884
Bert.

9
00:00:50.968 --> 00:00:52.469
Got anything new?

10
00:00:53.720 --> 00:00:54.805
Funny every time.

11
00:00:54.888 --> 00:00:57.683
(PORTAL HISSES. WARBLES)

12
00:00:57.766 --> 00:01:00.644
I think I'm ready to pull
the trigger on Batman 608.

13
00:01:01.645 --> 00:01:03.355
Excellent choice.

14
00:01:03.939 --> 00:01:05.107
What's the trade?

15
00:01:05.190 --> 00:01:08.735
What would you say
to a can of lima beans?

16
00:01:08.819 --> 00:01:12.072
Oh. geez. Bert. come on!
This is near mint.

17
00:01:12.114 --> 00:01:14.700
I could probably get a couple
Dinty Moore Beef Stews for this.

18
00:01:14.783 --> 00:01:15.993
Plus...

19
00:01:16.785 --> 00:01:18.245
cream corn.

20
00:01:18.328 --> 00:01:19.746
-Meh.
-BERT KIBBLER: Okay.

21
00:01:19.788 --> 00:01:23.000
I was saving it for my birthday.
but I guess I'll throw it in.

22
00:01:24.001 --> 00:01:25.502
Fancy Feast.

23
00:01:26.295 --> 00:01:27.254
What flavor?

24
00:01:27.337 --> 00:01:28.922
-Salmon.
-Sold.

25
00:01:29.006 --> 00:01:31.091
-Yay!
-TREVOR: Um. are you crazy?

26
00:01:31.174 --> 00:01:33.552
(SCOFFS) Hawkeye doesn't deserve
to be an Avenger.

27
00:01:33.635 --> 00:01:35.762
Yeah-- Whoa. whoa. whoa. whoa!
You do not want to go there.

28
00:01:35.804 --> 00:01:37.556
You got a guy
with a bow and arrow.

29
00:01:37.639 --> 00:01:39.266
and he's supposed to be
on the same team

30
00:01:39.308 --> 00:01:41.852
as a guy
with an arc reactor iron suit

31
00:01:41.935 --> 00:01:43.353
and the literal God of Thunder?

32
00:01:43.437 --> 00:01:45.022
(LAUGHS) What sense
does that even make?

33
00:01:45.105 --> 00:01:48.609
I don't know. I mean... (GRUNTS)
...does this make sense?

34
00:01:48.692 --> 00:01:51.570
-(SCREAMS. GROANS)
-♪ (UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING) ♪

35
00:01:51.612 --> 00:01:55.824
I just mopped!
We talked about this. Kyle!

36
00:01:55.907 --> 00:01:57.159
That's strike three!

37
00:01:57.242 --> 00:01:59.536
I'm sorry. okay?
Uh. but you heard him.

38
00:02:01.580 --> 00:02:03.415
Sorry. He started it.

39
00:02:04.249 --> 00:02:05.292
Unbelievable.

40
00:02:05.334 --> 00:02:07.586
-Give me a hand.
-BERT: Oh. yeah.

41
00:02:07.628 --> 00:02:10.464
You know. I feel the same way
about Green Arrow.

42
00:02:10.547 --> 00:02:12.883
Yeah. we all do but you don't
have to kill people.

43
00:02:13.467 --> 00:02:16.136
(PORTAL HISSES. WARBLES)

44
00:02:16.178 --> 00:02:17.971
(SIGHS) Bye!

45
00:02:18.013 --> 00:02:20.015
You ever wonder
where this thing goes?

46
00:02:20.098 --> 00:02:21.224
Nope.

47
00:02:21.308 --> 00:02:23.518
-Probably smart.
-TRAVELER: Stuart.

48
00:02:23.602 --> 00:02:25.646
♪ (INTRIGUING MUSIC PLAYING) ♪

49
00:02:25.687 --> 00:02:26.897
We gotta talk.

50
00:02:28.690 --> 00:02:30.651
Shit just got weird.

51
00:02:30.692 --> 00:02:34.321
♪ (THEME SONG PLAYING) ♪

52
00:02:35.197 --> 00:02:37.991
♪ Stuart tries
To reset our lives ♪

53
00:02:38.033 --> 00:02:41.328
♪ But he fails
To save the universe ♪

54
00:02:41.370 --> 00:02:44.498
♪ He's our only chance
And he tries and he tries ♪

55
00:02:44.539 --> 00:02:47.751
♪ But he fails
To save the universe ♪

56
00:02:49.086 --> 00:02:53.173
♪ (CHOIR VOCALIZING) ♪

57
00:03:01.098 --> 00:03:04.351
♪ Stuart fails ♪

58
00:03:04.434 --> 00:03:07.354
♪ (THEME SONG CONCLUDES) ♪

59
00:03:07.437 --> 00:03:09.272
Do you have
an identical twin brother?

60
00:03:09.356 --> 00:03:11.024
-♪ (SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING) ♪
-No.

61
00:03:11.066 --> 00:03:12.859
-Okay. I have two questions.
-Just two?

62
00:03:12.943 --> 00:03:14.861
I've only got a few seconds
to explain this.

63
00:03:14.903 --> 00:03:16.029
so you gotta focus.

64
00:03:16.071 --> 00:03:18.115
-Who are you?
-First question.

65
00:03:18.198 --> 00:03:20.909
I'm you from
another stream of reality.

66
00:03:20.992 --> 00:03:23.412
Well. that answers that.
Second question...

67
00:03:23.495 --> 00:03:25.205
Listen to me.

68
00:03:25.247 --> 00:03:28.542
This apocalyptic nightmare
that you are living in.

69
00:03:28.583 --> 00:03:30.877
it can be avoided.
it never has to happen.

70
00:03:30.919 --> 00:03:33.213
Okay. now I have.
like. six questions.

71
00:03:33.296 --> 00:03:35.465
-He can't be me.
-He looks like you.

72
00:03:35.549 --> 00:03:38.427
Senior prom. Emily Manhart.
peach schnapps.

73
00:03:38.510 --> 00:03:40.387
She was ready to go.
You puked in her lap.

74
00:03:40.470 --> 00:03:41.722
Sounds like you.

75
00:03:41.805 --> 00:03:43.265
At least I went
to my senior prom.

76
00:03:43.348 --> 00:03:45.684
I couldn't go. I had mono.

77
00:03:45.767 --> 00:03:47.602
Please. I don't have
a lot of time.

78
00:03:47.686 --> 00:03:50.397
Leonard Hofstadter.
Sheldon Cooper. Howard Wolowitz.

79
00:03:50.480 --> 00:03:52.733
-Remember them?
-Yeah. real nerds.

80
00:03:52.816 --> 00:03:54.067
Pot-kettle.

81
00:03:54.109 --> 00:03:55.777
-Sure.
-Fair enough.

82
00:03:55.861 --> 00:04:00.866
Anyway. they invented some kind
of quantum entanglement thing.

83
00:04:00.907 --> 00:04:02.743
and you were there
when it malfunctioned.

84
00:04:02.826 --> 00:04:04.035
Both of us or just him?

85
00:04:04.119 --> 00:04:06.163
-Doesn't matter!
-It matters to me.

86
00:04:06.246 --> 00:04:08.290
The point is.
it altered reality.

87
00:04:08.373 --> 00:04:09.958
None of this is supposed to be.

88
00:04:10.041 --> 00:04:12.419
And by none of this.
you mean...?

89
00:04:12.502 --> 00:04:13.545
None of it!

90
00:04:14.796 --> 00:04:19.342
The violence. the devastation.
the dimensional rifts!

91
00:04:19.426 --> 00:04:22.304
-Dimensional rifts!
-Now we know.

92
00:04:22.387 --> 00:04:24.639
None of this is normal.

93
00:04:27.142 --> 00:04:29.269
-Certainly not that!
-The big moth?

94
00:04:29.352 --> 00:04:32.439
(SCOFFS) Yes! Yes! The big moth!

95
00:04:32.522 --> 00:04:34.983
If you turn the lights off.
they don't bother you.

96
00:04:36.777 --> 00:04:39.362
You can put everything right.
You can make it the way it was.

97
00:04:39.446 --> 00:04:41.364
-You just have to find the--
-Hang on.

98
00:04:41.448 --> 00:04:42.908
-Hang on!
-♪ (INTRIGUING MUSIC PLAYING) ♪

99
00:04:42.949 --> 00:04:45.202
If you're me
from another reality.

100
00:04:45.285 --> 00:04:46.828
how can you be in this one?

101
00:04:46.912 --> 00:04:48.955
I don't know.
I'm not a quantum physicist.

102
00:04:48.997 --> 00:04:50.791
I went to the Rhode Island
School of Design.

103
00:04:50.832 --> 00:04:53.210
-I didn't know that.
-Oh. yeah. I have a BFA.

104
00:04:53.293 --> 00:04:55.462
Really? How come
you never did anything with it?

105
00:04:55.504 --> 00:04:56.922
What am I gonna do.
teach high school kids

106
00:04:57.005 --> 00:04:59.508
-how to draw fruit?
-(SIGHS) Guys. please!

107
00:04:59.591 --> 00:05:02.469
The machine is still at Caltech.
Here's what you have to do.

108
00:05:02.552 --> 00:05:04.179
Hang on. let me write this down.

109
00:05:04.262 --> 00:05:06.681
♪ (QUIRKY SUSPENSEFUL
MUSIC PLAYING) ♪

110
00:05:06.765 --> 00:05:08.433
"Cal... "

111
00:05:08.517 --> 00:05:10.143
Oh. shoot!

112
00:05:10.185 --> 00:05:13.313
-What is shaking it gonna do?
-Stop talking and listen.

113
00:05:13.396 --> 00:05:15.857
You know. I might have
a Sharpie. excuse me.

114
00:05:17.192 --> 00:05:19.820
-Listen!
-♪ (DRAMATIC MUSICAL STING) ♪

115
00:05:19.903 --> 00:05:21.404
When you get to the machine...

116
00:05:21.488 --> 00:05:23.907
-(GARBLED SPEECH)
-♪ (MYSTERIOUS MUSIC PLAYING) ♪

117
00:05:23.990 --> 00:05:25.700
-Damn it!
-W... What's happening?

118
00:05:25.784 --> 00:05:26.827
I don't know!

119
00:05:26.910 --> 00:05:29.579
I'm going through
some kind of wormhole!

120
00:05:29.663 --> 00:05:32.249
(GROANS)
The important thing is...

121
00:05:32.332 --> 00:05:35.585
(GARBLED SPEECH)

122
00:05:35.669 --> 00:05:37.754
And... And when you find him...

123
00:05:37.838 --> 00:05:39.589
(GARBLED SPEECH)

124
00:05:40.757 --> 00:05:43.677
...and that will fix everything.

125
00:05:43.760 --> 00:05:46.054
(WHOOSHING WARBLE)

126
00:05:48.348 --> 00:05:50.308
You get any of that?

127
00:05:50.392 --> 00:05:52.727
-I got the gist.
-♪ (MUSIC FADES) ♪

128
00:05:52.811 --> 00:05:54.563
-♪ (INTENSE MUSIC PLAYING) ♪
-(DOG BARKING)

129
00:05:54.646 --> 00:05:56.690
(BARKS. GROWLS)

130
00:05:56.773 --> 00:05:58.650
(GROWLS. SNARLS)

131
00:05:58.733 --> 00:06:00.026
-(WANDERER GRUNTS)
-(TEETH CRUNCH)

132
00:06:00.110 --> 00:06:01.194
(DOG WHIMPERS)

133
00:06:01.236 --> 00:06:02.904
Nice catch. Steve!

134
00:06:02.988 --> 00:06:04.573
How is it out there?

135
00:06:04.656 --> 00:06:06.992
It's a little nippy.
Wear layers.

136
00:06:07.075 --> 00:06:08.994
-(DOOR RATTLES)
-(KEYS JANGLING)

137
00:06:10.078 --> 00:06:11.162
Shall we?

138
00:06:11.246 --> 00:06:15.041
(SIGHS) Mm. I don't know.
I'm having second thoughts.

139
00:06:15.083 --> 00:06:17.836
What are you talking about?
We've been given a quest.

140
00:06:17.919 --> 00:06:19.880
Yeah. but. uh.
do we believe that guy?

141
00:06:19.921 --> 00:06:21.214
That guy was you.

142
00:06:21.298 --> 00:06:22.257
That's my point.

143
00:06:22.340 --> 00:06:24.718
When did we start listening
to me?

144
00:06:24.759 --> 00:06:27.220
Maybe we have a chance
to fix the world.

145
00:06:27.262 --> 00:06:29.139
I don't know.
I think it's important
to ask the question.

146
00:06:29.222 --> 00:06:31.099
Is this reality that bad?

147
00:06:31.182 --> 00:06:32.309
(ZOMBIE GROWLS)

148
00:06:32.392 --> 00:06:33.310
(ZOMBIE GROANS)

149
00:06:33.393 --> 00:06:35.395
I think there's room
for improvement.

150
00:06:35.437 --> 00:06:39.608
♪ (FUNKY TENSE MUSIC PLAYING) ♪

151
00:06:40.775 --> 00:06:44.529
(SCAVENGERS GRUNTING)

152
00:06:45.280 --> 00:06:46.865
What are you doing?

153
00:06:46.948 --> 00:06:49.200
What's it look like?
I'm trying to get us to Caltech.

154
00:06:49.284 --> 00:06:51.077
With a Thomas Guide?

155
00:06:51.119 --> 00:06:53.622
I would've used
the GPS on my iPhone.

156
00:06:53.705 --> 00:06:55.916
but civilization
seemed to have collapsed.

157
00:06:55.957 --> 00:06:57.417
-(RAT SQUEALS. CHOMPS)
-PENN: Ow!

158
00:06:57.500 --> 00:06:58.668
Check it out.

159
00:06:58.752 --> 00:07:00.670
♪ (JAUNTY CARNIVAL MUSIC
PLAYING OVER SPEAKERS) ♪

160
00:07:00.754 --> 00:07:01.922
-Juggling two-- (YELPS)
-(RAT CHOMPS)

161
00:07:02.005 --> 00:07:05.467
Juggling two starving
feral creatures.

162
00:07:05.550 --> 00:07:08.094
as. uh. you can see.
is not difficult. but...

163
00:07:08.178 --> 00:07:09.429
-(RATS SQUEALING. CHOMPING)
-(GROANS)

164
00:07:09.512 --> 00:07:14.476
...juggling three is... (GRUNTS)
...profoundly stupid. Ow!

165
00:07:14.559 --> 00:07:15.810
(GRUNTS)

166
00:07:15.894 --> 00:07:17.646
I saw them in Vegas.

167
00:07:17.729 --> 00:07:19.522
-Such a fun night.
-Oh.

168
00:07:19.606 --> 00:07:22.442
You know who I loved in Vegas
and I didn't think I would?

169
00:07:22.484 --> 00:07:24.235
-Huh?
-Celine Dion.

170
00:07:24.319 --> 00:07:26.488
Mm. Oh. I'm sorry.

171
00:07:26.571 --> 00:07:29.658
-(RATS SQUEALING)
-(PENN GRUNTS. GROANS)

172
00:07:32.160 --> 00:07:33.161
Oh. all right.

173
00:07:34.412 --> 00:07:35.914
-(RAT CHOMPS)
-(GROANS) Yeah.

174
00:07:35.997 --> 00:07:37.874
(GRUNTS)

175
00:07:40.835 --> 00:07:42.128
(EXHALES)

176
00:07:42.212 --> 00:07:43.254
Thank you!

177
00:07:43.338 --> 00:07:44.923
-We are Penn and Teller...
-(AUDIENCE APPLAUDING)

178
00:07:45.006 --> 00:07:47.300
...and we'll be here
until we're dead!

179
00:07:47.384 --> 00:07:49.344
-(RATS SQUEALING)
-(PENN GRUNTS)

180
00:07:49.427 --> 00:07:52.180
-(FLIES BUZZING)
-♪ (DARK TECHNO MUSIC PLAYING) ♪

181
00:07:52.263 --> 00:07:55.976
(INDISTINCT CHATTER)

182
00:07:56.059 --> 00:07:57.727
(PORTAL HISSES. WARBLES)

183
00:08:03.942 --> 00:08:06.653
-Moth.
-(CROWD GASPING)

184
00:08:06.736 --> 00:08:09.656
(INDISTINCT CHATTER)

185
00:08:09.739 --> 00:08:13.493
Oh. my God. look. Floss.

186
00:08:13.576 --> 00:08:15.495
BERT: Just hurry.
It's getting dark.

187
00:08:15.578 --> 00:08:16.663
STUART BLOOM: Yeah. yeah. yeah.

188
00:08:16.705 --> 00:08:19.666
Excuse me. uh. how much
for a foot of floss?

189
00:08:19.708 --> 00:08:21.960
-Mint or regular?
-Uh. let me get the regular.

190
00:08:22.043 --> 00:08:23.003
VENDOR: Oh.

191
00:08:23.044 --> 00:08:25.171
♪ (OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING) ♪

192
00:08:25.255 --> 00:08:28.758
♪ (INTRIGUING MUSICAL STING) ♪

193
00:08:28.842 --> 00:08:31.469
Thank you.
Oh. yeah. look at that.

194
00:08:32.303 --> 00:08:34.264
Can't put a price
on healthy gums.

195
00:08:37.017 --> 00:08:39.853
Oh! Oh. this feels so good.

196
00:08:39.894 --> 00:08:41.896
Go easy. We're sharing that.

197
00:08:42.731 --> 00:08:43.898
(GUN COCKS)

198
00:08:44.691 --> 00:08:45.817
Not a good sound.

199
00:08:49.070 --> 00:08:50.321
Stuart?

200
00:08:51.823 --> 00:08:52.866
Denise?

201
00:08:52.907 --> 00:08:54.325
I thought you were dead.
(CHUCKLES)

202
00:08:54.409 --> 00:08:56.745
-I thought you were dead!
-Aw!

203
00:08:56.828 --> 00:08:59.039
So. what have you been up to?

204
00:08:59.122 --> 00:09:00.206
Robbing mostly.

205
00:09:00.290 --> 00:09:01.541
Still working on my screenplay.

206
00:09:01.624 --> 00:09:03.752
-Oh. good for you.
-Yeah. How have you been?

207
00:09:03.835 --> 00:09:06.421
-Okay. Still got the store.
-Oh. that's great.

208
00:09:06.504 --> 00:09:08.131
What's going on?

209
00:09:08.214 --> 00:09:09.716
Don't worry. Gary.
I know these guys.

210
00:09:09.799 --> 00:09:11.259
So. we're not robbing.
we're not killing?

211
00:09:11.342 --> 00:09:12.260
What are we doing?

212
00:09:12.343 --> 00:09:13.636
DENISE: You remember
I mentioned Stuart?

213
00:09:13.720 --> 00:09:16.222
Oh. sure. How's it going? Gary.

214
00:09:16.264 --> 00:09:17.265
Hi.

215
00:09:18.266 --> 00:09:20.018
So. are you two...?

216
00:09:20.060 --> 00:09:22.187
You gotta remember.
I thought you were dead.

217
00:09:22.270 --> 00:09:24.189
Yeah. no. right. right. yeah.

218
00:09:24.272 --> 00:09:26.649
Funny story. actually. uh.
Gary was seeing my friend Lisa.

219
00:09:26.733 --> 00:09:28.234
Oh. nice girl. Yeah. Jewish.

220
00:09:28.318 --> 00:09:31.654
Yeah. and anyway. Lisa got eaten
by cannibals in Sherman Oaks.

221
00:09:31.738 --> 00:09:33.448
-Oh. no.
-DENISE: Mm-hmm.

222
00:09:33.531 --> 00:09:36.743
Human meat isn't kosher.
but I guess that only matters

223
00:09:36.826 --> 00:09:38.870
if the cannibals
are also Jewish.

224
00:09:41.498 --> 00:09:44.167
Anyway. we. um. you know.
comforted each other.

225
00:09:44.250 --> 00:09:45.877
The lady has skills. am I right?

226
00:09:45.960 --> 00:09:47.420
Well...

227
00:09:47.504 --> 00:09:51.132
To be honest. I mostly focused
on my own performance.

228
00:09:52.550 --> 00:09:54.135
Anyway. uh. we gotta go.

229
00:09:54.219 --> 00:09:56.805
Yeah. Caltech. We're on a quest.

230
00:09:56.888 --> 00:09:58.598
-♪ (OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING) ♪
-There's no more Caltech.

231
00:09:58.640 --> 00:09:59.933
What's left of it
is a death trap.

232
00:09:59.974 --> 00:10:01.101
We don't have a choice.

233
00:10:01.142 --> 00:10:03.645
Yeah. an alternate version of me
came from another universe

234
00:10:03.728 --> 00:10:05.688
and explained
how I can undo the apocalypse.

235
00:10:05.772 --> 00:10:07.607
It was really cool.

236
00:10:07.690 --> 00:10:09.109
An alternate version of you?

237
00:10:09.150 --> 00:10:11.528
Yeah. same pasty face
and same whiny voice.

238
00:10:11.611 --> 00:10:12.946
It was like looking in a mirror.

239
00:10:13.029 --> 00:10:15.323
-Well. good luck.
-♪ (MUSIC TURNS DARING) ♪

240
00:10:15.406 --> 00:10:18.493
-Yeah. nice to see you.
-Yeah. you too.

241
00:10:18.576 --> 00:10:21.538
Have fun with
the... looting and stuff.

242
00:10:22.747 --> 00:10:23.748
Ciao.

243
00:10:26.251 --> 00:10:27.460
(GARY SIGHS)

244
